## Current Status
Backdrop CSS confirmed: both `assets/css/style.css` and `assets/css/inner.css` use `display: none` / `display: block` toggling. The full backdrop CSS properties (position, inset, z-index, background) were not yet read — need to read those lines to confirm exact values and diagnose the click-blocking bug. The backdrop is covering the entire viewport including the sidebar menu area, which is why clicks on menu items are blocked. The fix is to ensure the sidebar (`z-index: 99999`) is above the backdrop (`z-index: 99998`) — if it already is, the issue may be something else in the CSS (e.g., missing z-index on the menu, or a stacking context problem).
